completed_at: "2026-11-13T21:04:26.321Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 90
acceptance_criteria: "A passing, trusted, mismatch-free pm test --run row returns no raw ANSI escape sequences and at most a bounded stdout tail in TOON and JSON; Failing, refused, skipped and mismatched rows keep their full captured output; An explicit selector restores the full output on every row, and the omission receipt names it"
parent: pm-5t33or
risk: low
confidence: high
severity: low
resolution: "src/core/output/linked-test-projection.ts keeps, for a quiet run (every row passed, mismatch-free, zero failure categories), an escape-free tail of each trusted row's stdout/stderr: stripVTControlCharacters, carriage-return overwrites collapsed, blank lines dropped, at most 6 lines and 480 code points. A shortened row gains <stream>_omitted_bytes; omission_receipt appends run_results.stdout/stderr with restore_with --full-output. Failing, refused, skipped, mismatched rows, every row of a non-quiet run, and rows that passed only under an untrusted override keep complete output. --full-output is registered on pm test (requires --run) and pm test-all, mirrored as MCP fullOutput (schema 4.26.0), completion, flag contracts and budgets (test 58, test-all 41). SDK and MCP results are unchanged (pm-py5fam tracks MCP)."
expected_result: "A passing, trusted, mismatch-free row returns no ANSI escapes and at most a bounded tail; failing/refused/skipped/mismatched rows keep full output; an explicit selector restores full output and the omission receipt names it"
actual_result: "Verified by tests/unit/core/output/linked-test-projection.spec.ts (7 cases: tail, untrusted override, stderr and receipt merge, terminal reduction, non-quiet variants, --full-output) and dogfood: pm test pm-v1mp64 --run returned a 6-line escape-free tail with stdout_omitted_bytes 355"
